.TH ZERODDS-GRPC-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-grpc-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-grpc-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/grpc-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the gRPC bridge daemon exposes DDS topics as gRPC
services. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-grpc-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the parser that reads it is
.I parse_yaml_subset
in
.IR crates/grpc-bridge/src/bin/zerodds-grpc-bridged.rs .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " grpc ", " auth ", " metrics ", " topics .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr naming the key and the
expected set, then starts with the defaults \(em watch the WARN log.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
A
.B \-\-log\-level
on the command line wins over this key.
.SS grpc
.TP
.B bind
HTTP/2 listen address, e.g.
.IR "0.0.0.0:50051" .
.TP
.B tls
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean) and the server material
.BR cert_file " / " key_file ,
PEM, readable by user
.IR zerodds .
ALPN is
.IR h2 .
.B client_ca_file
names the CA for client certificates;
.B require_client_cert
(boolean, default false) makes a client without a certificate fail the
handshake. With
.B enabled
and no
.BR cert_file / key_file
the daemon does not start (exit 4).
.TP
.B reflection
Sub-map with
.BR enabled .
Turns on
.IR grpc.reflection.v1alpha ;
the admin
.I /catalog
mirrors the same topic set.
.SS auth
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " bearer " | " jwt " | " mtls " (\(sc7.2),"
checked on every call; a failed check is
.IR UNAUTHENTICATED .
A mode whose input is missing stops the start.
.TP
.BR bearer_token ", " bearer_subject
For
.IR bearer :
the token in the
.I authorization
metadata
.RI ( "Bearer <token>" )
and the subject it stands for (default
.IR anonymous ).
.TP
.B jwt
Sub-map for
.BR jwt :
.B public_key
(PEM file, PKCS#1 or SubjectPublicKeyInfo, RS256),
.BR issuer ,
.BR audience ,
.B required_claim
.RI ( claim=value ;
a space-separated claim such as
.I scope
matches when it contains the value).
.I exp
and
.I nbf
are enforced with 60 s leeway. The subject is the
.I sub
claim.
.PP
For
.IR mtls ,
.B grpc.tls.enabled
and
.B grpc.tls.client_ca_file
are required; the subject is the client certificate's subject DN (RFC 4514,
such as
.IR CN=alice,O=Example );
an ACL entry may name its fingerprint
.I mtls:<SHA-256 hex>
instead.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9095"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
.SS topics (list)
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B grpc_service
Name of the generated gRPC service.
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries
.B Publish
calls into DDS (the daemon creates a DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to
.B Subscribe
calls (a DataReader),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
A call against the direction a topic does not carry ends with
.B FAILED_PRECONDITION
(9); a failed DDS write with
.B UNAVAILABLE
(14).
.TP
.B acl
Sub-map with
.B publish
and
.B subscribe
(lists of subjects,
.I *
for all,
.I *group:<g>*
for a JWT group), \(sc7.3.
.B Publish
needs
.BR publish ,
.B Subscribe
needs
.BR subscribe ;
otherwise the call is
.IR PERMISSION_DENIED .
Without any
.B acl
every topic is open under
.BI "auth.mode: " none
and closed under every other mode; with one, a topic without an entry is
closed.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/grpc-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-grpc-bridged (1).
